usage: windows-probe.py [-h] --host HOST --identity IDENTITY --exe EXE
                        [--test-metadata TEST_METADATA]
                        [--test-timeout-seconds TEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS]
                        [--native-seconds NATIVE_SECONDS] [--system-host]
                        [--audio-silent] [--materials] [--autostart]
                        [--calendar] [--calendar-download] [--application]
                        [--web-voice] [--web-pairing] --report REPORT

Run only supplied development probes in a disposable remote Windows directory.
Credentials stay outside the repository. Existing SSH configuration is
retained.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --host HOST
  --identity IDENTITY
  --exe EXE
  --test-metadata TEST_METADATA
  --test-timeout-seconds TEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
                        per supplied test EXE budget in seconds (1..900;
                        default 60)
  --native-seconds NATIVE_SECONDS
  --system-host         also run new read-only system and interactive hidden-
                        host probes
  --audio-silent        zero PCM only; no volume/microphone/foreground changes
  --materials           run synthetic file/validation/SQLite/private Shell
                        receiver integration
  --autostart           isolated hidden native durable startup settings;
                        generated scratch Registry leaf only
  --calendar            isolated hidden native calendar candidate
                        review/adoption/policy/CAS; synthetic feed
  --calendar-download   one fixed2026 WinHTTP HTTPS feed request; no
                        application writes
  --application         exercise the actual workbench in an isolated hidden
                        test deployment
  --web-voice           interactive hidden-task authenticated voice
                        upload/jobs and native zero-PCM three-repeat/cancel
                        integration
  --web-pairing         noninteractive CNG/DPAPI/SQLite pairing and synthetic
                        trusted-TLS metadata port probe; no HTTPS
                        listener/browser
  --report REPORT
